  "id": "Compound::DB01351 - Gene::2554",
  "verbalization": "Amobarbital is likely to interact with Gabra1 through a shared pathway involving Gaba-a Receptor Activity. The evidence suggests that Amobarbital binds to Gabra3, Gabra2, or Gabra5, all of which participate in Gaba-a Receptor Activity, which in turn is participated by Gabra1. This indicates a potential mechanism where Amobarbital may influence Gabra1 through a common intermediate, Gaba-a Receptor Activity. The varying target proteins (Gabra2, Gabra3, and Gabra5) suggest that Amobarbital may have multiple binding sites or that the receptor activity is modulated by different isoforms. The high scores in the paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
